Hi,<div><br></div><div>I just transferred my JAGS code of modeling the multinomial probabilities into NIMBLE. I have confirmed that my NIMBLE installation steps are correct, but it still reports <b>&quot;Error: Failed to create the shared library.&quot;</b> I have also tried a similar Binomial model. It CAN work in NIMBLE without any errors. So, I just wonder which step in this multinomial version code might involve issues.</div><div><br></div><div>I want to ask for your helps about troubleshooting. A runnable sample code is provided below. I will appreciate a lot if anyone wants to have a try and share some ideas about any potential problems :)</div><div><br></div><div>#some data and constants</div><div>Y &lt;- cbind(c(93, 97, 91, 94, 92, 92, 91, 96, 97, 87, 90, 97, 92, 82, 96, 83, 94, 83, 93, 87, 93, 92, 96, 88, 95, 92, 94, 84, 91, 89), c(6, 3, 6, 5, 7, 6, 6, 2, 2, 11, 6, 1, 7, 15, 4, 14, 4, 12, 5, 10, 4, 5, 4, 10, 3, 7, 3, 13, 5, 9), c(1, 0, 3, 1, 1, 2, 3, 2, 1, 2, 4, 2, 1, 3, 0, 3, 2, 5, 2, 3, 3, 3, 0, 2, 2, 1, 3, 3, 4, 2))<br>N &lt;- rep(100, 30)<br>study &lt;- rep(1:15, each=2)<br>trt &lt;- c(rep(c(1,2), 5), rep(c(1,3), 5), rep(c(2,3), 5))<br>  <br># model building<br>model &lt;- nimbleCode({<br>  for (j in 1:J){  <br>    Y[j,1:3] ~ dmulti(theta.adj[j,1:3], N[j])<br>     <br>    theta.adj[j,1:3] &lt;- max(0.00001, min(theta[j,1:3], 0.99999))<br>     <br>    theta[j,1] &lt;- 1/(1+rr21[j]+rr31[j])<br>    theta[j,2] &lt;- rr21[j]/(1+rr21[j]+rr31[j])<br>    theta[j,3] &lt;- rr31[j]/(1+rr21[j]+rr31[j])<br>    <br>    log(rr21[j]) &lt;- alpha1[study[j]] + beta1[trt[j]]<br>    log(rr31[j]) &lt;- alpha2[study[j]] + beta2[trt[j]]<br>  }<br>  #prior specifications<br>  for (i1 in 1:n.study){<br>    alpha1[i1] ~ dnorm(mu.study1, sd=sigma.study1)<br>    alpha2[i1] ~ dnorm(mu.study2, sd=sigma.study2)<br>  }<br>  mu.study1 ~ dnorm(0, 0.0001)<br>  mu.study2 ~ dnorm(0, 0.0001)<br>  sigma.study1 ~ T(dt(0, a, 1), 0,)<br>  sigma.study2 ~ T(dt(0, a, 1), 0,)<br><br>  for (i2 in 1:n.trt){<br>    beta1[i2] ~ dnorm(mu.trt1, sd=sigma.trt1)<br>    beta2[i2] ~ dnorm(mu.trt2, sd=sigma.trt2)<br>  }<br>  mu.trt1 ~ dnorm(0, 0.0001)<br>  mu.trt2 ~ dnorm(0, 0.0001)<br>  sigma.trt1 ~ T(dt(0, a, 1), 0,)<br>  sigma.trt2 ~ T(dt(0, a, 1), 0,)<br><br>  rr21_ov &lt;- exp( mean(alpha1[1:n.study]) + mean(beta1[1:n.trt]) )<br>  rr31_ov &lt;- exp( mean(alpha2[1:n.study]) + mean(beta2[1:n.trt]) )<br>  p1_ov &lt;- 1/(1+rr21_ov+rr31_ov)<br>  p2_ov &lt;- rr21_ov/(1+rr21_ov+rr31_ov)<br>  p3_ov &lt;- rr31_ov/(1+rr21_ov+rr31_ov)<br>})<br><br>consts &lt;- list(N=N, J=30, study=study, trt=trt, <br>               a=0.0016, n.study=15, n.trt=3)<br>data &lt;- list(Y=Y)<br>initials &lt;- list(alpha1=rep(-1, 15), mu.study1=-1, sigma.study1=0.05,<br>                 alpha2=rep(-1, 15), mu.study2=-1, sigma.study2=0.05,<br>                 beta1=rep(-1, 3), mu.trt1=-1, sigma.trt1=0.05,<br>                 beta2=rep(-1, 3), mu.trt2=-1, sigma.trt2=0.05)<br>rModel &lt;- nimbleModel(code=model, data=data, inits=initials, constants=consts)<br><br>cModel &lt;- compileNimble(rModel)<br></div><div>## error will be produced after this command. It seems that it reports some error in C++, for which I nearly know nothing. </div><div>&quot;printErrors()&quot; will show: </div><div><br></div><div>P_3_model_MID_3_nfCode.cpp: In member function &#39;virtual void theta_dot_adj_L3_UID_57::simulate(const indexedNodeInfo&amp;) const&#39;:
P_3_model_MID_3_nfCode.cpp:277:381: error: cannot convert &#39;Eigen::Transpose&lt;Eigen::Block&lt;Eigen::Map&lt;Eigen::Matrix&lt;double, -1, -1&gt;, 0, Eigen::Stride&lt;0, 0&gt; &gt;, -1, -1, false&gt; &gt;&#39; to &#39;double&#39;
  277 | ((eigenBlock_oPmodel_theta_dot_adj_comma_getNodeFunctionIndexedInfo_oPARG1_INDEXEDNODEINFO___comma_1_cP_comma_1to3_cP).block(ARG1_INDEXEDNODEINFO__.info[0] - 1, 0, 1, 3)).transpose() = pairmax(1e-05, pairmin(((eigenBlock_oPmodel_theta_comma_getNodeFunctionIndexedInfo_oPARG1_INDEXEDNODEINFO___comma_1_cP_comma_1to3_cP).block(ARG1_INDEXEDNODEINFO__.info[0] - 1, 0, 1, 3)).transpose(), 0.99999));
      |                                                                                                                                                                                                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^~  ETC.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Again, thanks for anyone who might be interested in this problem or have similar issues. Any free discussions are also welcome.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>TT</div>
